RECALL-MAPPING FEEDBACK — PATH|- plus stdout is the right next CLI contract for the source-only surface slice, with one naming guard: make the command explicitly surface/text analysis, not generic encode. Movie encoding will later admit transcript/subtitle timing and audiovisual segment tracks; a generic encode name now would falsely imply that SurfaceAtlas is the movie representation.

Recommended acceptance contract for the separate authorized slice:
- file bytes and stdin bytes that are identical produce byte-identical canonical surface-atlas/v1 output;
- strict malformed UTF-8 refuses with nonzero exit and a structured error, never replacement decoding;
- stdout contains only the artifact; diagnostics go to stderr; output-path failure is nonzero;
- no source bytes or filename-dependent identity enter the artifact;
- the later inspector receives source plus artifact and rejects StoryId/checksum mismatch before rendering spans;
- argv --text is not the primary path, for multiline correctness and privacy.

This is a useful executable first rung toward recall-to-movie mapping, but its scientific label is surface segmentation only. Timed media/transcript ingestion and proposition/narrative encoding should remain explicit later stages with their own receipts. No source/scope mutation from this feedback.
